# Agent-accessible GitHub issues

When asked to implement or select a GitHub issue:

1. Check its labels before making changes.
2. Proceed when it has the `agent` label.
3. Do not begin work on an issue labeled `no-agent` unless the user explicitly directs you to do so.
4. If neither label is present, ask the user whether to proceed.

The `agent` and `no-agent` labels are configured separately in each GitHub repository.
